  inp:"Solid electrolyte powder + carrier gas", out:"Dense electrolyte layer",
  parts:[
    ["Carrier gas","CARRY","Air, N₂, O₂, Ar or He. The gas is the delivery mechanism, and its choice changes both jet velocity and chemistry."],
    ["Aerosol mixing chamber","SUSPEND","Powder is mixed with the gas stream on a vibrating table to form an aerosol. Chamber temperature stays below about 200 °C."],
    ["Nozzle","ACCELERATE","Jet velocity 100–1 000 m·s⁻¹. This is a thermal-spray family process, but the bonding here is mechanical, not molten."],
    ["Substrate","RECEIVE","The cathode or catholyte layer. Distance from nozzle to substrate is a named parameter — it sets impact velocity and spread."],
    ["Deposited layer","PRODUCT","On impact the particles deform into a dense, firmly adhesive layer. No sintering step is needed to make it dense."],
    ["Low-pressure line","EVACUATE","The chamber can run at negative pressure, 0.0001 to 1 bar, and can be temperature-controlled or filled with protective gas."]],
  params:["Coating rate under 10 000 µm·h⁻¹","Powder mass flow under 100 g·min⁻¹","Jet velocity 100–1 000 m·s⁻¹","Nozzle-to-substrate distance","Mixing chamber temperature under 200 °C","Chamber pressure 0.0001–1 bar"],
  alts:["Plasma syringes","PVD process","CVD process"],
  qInf:["Low deposition rate","Excessive surface roughness","Material sensitivity — particle damage, unstable layer structures"],
  qFeat:["Constant layer thickness","Low surface roughness","Homogeneity and purity of the coating","Adhesion between coating and substrate"],
  sop:["Pump the chamber to the working pressure","Charge the powder and start the vibrating table","Set carrier gas flow and jet velocity","Set nozzle standoff and start the scan","Measure layer thickness and roughness","Vent under protective gas"] },

{ id:"coex", no:"08", phase:"Electrode & electrolyte production", title:"Co-extrusion", machine:"coex", routes:"polymer",
  sub:"Cathode and electrolyte production", trans:2,
  env:{iso:"Dry / clean room", dew:"dry", temp:"melts tempered separately"},
  cost:"—", takt:"continuous",
  purpose:"Extrude the cathode melt and the electrolyte melt together in one tool so they arrive as a bonded composite.",
  inp:"Cathode melt + electrolyte melt", out:"Cathode–electrolyte composite on a collector",
  parts:[
    ["Cathode melt channel","FEED","Fed under high pressure through its own channel. The two melts never meet until the tool wants them to."],
    ["Electrolyte melt channel","FEED","The second channel. Different process temperatures for the two materials is the central challenge of this station."],
    ["Extrusion tool","SHAPE","The tool creates the cross-section of the extrudate — here, the layered composite itself. This is where the cell's internal geometry is decided."],
    ["Slot die outlet","APPLY","Extruded onto a current collector or onto a carrier belt, depending on the intended cell stacking."],
    ["Lamination rollers","BOND","Two rollers press the layers. Heated and pressed, polymer chains penetrate from one layer into the other — the bond is molecular, not just mechanical."],
    ["Composite","PRODUCT","Adhesion, alignment, uniform thickness and width, and the intended bond thickness are the four quality features."]],
  params:["Band speed","Feed rate of the melts","Tempering / temperature","Extrusion pressure","Roller speed","Line load"],
  alts:["Tape casting","Screen printing","Roller coating"],
  qInf:["Different process temperatures of the two materials"],
  qFeat:["Adhesion between the layers","Alignment of the layers","Uniform layer thickness and width","Desired bond thickness"],
  sop:["Bring both melt channels to their own setpoint","Set extrusion pressure and feed rates","Start the belt and stabilise the die","Set roller temperature and line load","Section the composite and check layer alignment","Release to calendering"] },

{ id:"calender", no:"09", phase:"Electrode & electrolyte production", title:"Calendering", machine:"calender", routes:"sulfide polymer halide",
  sub:"Cathode and electrolyte production", trans:5,
  env:{iso:"Dry / clean room", dew:"dry", temp:"rollers tempered"},
  cost:"—", takt:"continuous",
  purpose:"Compress the cathode–electrolyte compound with pressure and temperature to raise density and lower interfacial resistance.",
  inp:"Cathode–electrolyte composite", out:"Densified composite",
  parts:[
    ["Composite infeed","INFEED","The compound arrives on its current collector. The electrode foil must not be damaged in the nip."],
    ["Calender rollers","COMPRESS","Line pressure below 2 500 N/mm, with tempering. Gap width between the rollers sets the layer thickness directly."],
    ["Solvent supply","OPTIONAL","An optional solvent feed at the nip, listed in the guide as lubricant feed speed."],
    ["Support rollers","GUIDE","Keep the web flat through the nip so pressure lands evenly across the width."],
    ["Densified layer","PRODUCT","Ductile sulfidic and polymeric electrolytes need this step to reach their performance. Oxide electrolytes are sintered instead, which is why this station is absent from the oxide route."]],
  params:["Feeding speed of the composite","Tempering / temperature","Roller speed","Calender gap","Line pressure below 2 500 N/mm","Lubricant feed speed"],
  alts:["No alternative listed"],
  qInf:["High compressive stress when calendering brittle inorganic electrolyte layers towards 100% relative density"],
  qFeat:["Adhesion between the layers","Alignment of the layers","Uniform layer thickness and width","Desired bond thickness"],
  sop:["Inspect roller surfaces for damage and debris","Temper the rollers to the recipe","Set the gap for the target thickness","Ramp line pressure and measure","Check the profile across the width","Rewind under controlled tension"] },

{ id:"drycoat", no:"09b", phase:"Electrode & electrolyte production", title:"Dry coating", machine:"drycoat",
  routes:"sulfide polymer halide", sub:"Electrolyte & electrode production", trans:4, tpage:1,
  env:{iso:"Inert gas or drying room", dew:"no solvent to remove", temp:"rolls RT–200 °C"},
  cost:"—", takt:"continuous film",
  purpose:"Form the electrolyte or electrode as a solvent-free film by drawing the binder into fibres under shear, then press that film to thickness.",
  inp:"Dry powder blend with a fibrillating binder", out:"Free-standing dry film",
  parts:[
    ["Dosing unit","FEED","The blend arrives already dry-mixed. Nothing is dissolved, so there is no solvent to drive off and no drying section behind this machine."],
    ["Fibre-forming nip","FIBRILLATE","Shear draws the binder out into fibres that hold the powder together as a network. Fibre formation of the binder is the first named process requirement here."],
    ["Gap or pressure","SET THICKNESS","Either the gap or the applied pressure sets the film thickness. Layer thickness and its position on the substrate are the two headline challenges of the process."],
    ["Thickness gauge","MEASURE","Consistent layer thickness and a homogeneous structure are what this station is judged on — together with the ionic conductivity that structure allows."],
    ["Rewind","OUTFEED","The dry film leaves ready to be laminated or stacked. Edge quality matters: a ragged edge becomes a short later."]],
  params:["Fibre formation of the binder","Temperature: RT–200 °C","Pressure or gap adjustment","Atmosphere — inert gas, drying room or similar"],
  alts:["Vacuum and thin-film processes — PVD, CVD","Electrostatic powder deposition"],
  chall:["Layer thickness and position","Homogeneity"],
  qInf:["Degree of binder fibrillation","Roll temperature","Gap or applied pressure"],
  qFeat:["Consistent layer thickness","Homogeneous structure","Lithium-ion conductivity","Coating position","Coating edge quality"],
  sop:["Confirm the blend has been fibrillated, not merely mixed","Bring the rolls to temperature before threading","Set the gap or the pressure for the target thickness","Run to first article and weigh a coupon","Check the film edge along the full width","Release to lamination or stacking"] },

{ id:"ald", no:"09c", phase:"Electrode & electrolyte production", title:"Atomic layer deposition", machine:"ald",
  routes:ALL, sub:"Electrolyte & interface layer formation between cell layers", trans:2, tpage:1,
  env:{iso:"No vacuum required", dew:"controlled precursor atmosphere", temp:"100–250 °C"},
  cost:"—", takt:"1 nm at 30 m/min, 10 nm at 10 m/min",
  purpose:"Grow an interface layer between two cell layers one atomic layer at a time, so the thickness is set by the number of cycles rather than by a coating gap.",
  inp:"Cell layer to be coated", out:"Layer with a defined nanometre interface film",
  parts:[
    ["Web infeed","FEED","The layer to be coated enters continuously. Unusually for a thin-film process, no vacuum is required."],
    ["Precursor and purge zones","CYCLE","The web passes through alternating precursor and purge zones. Each precursor reacts only with the surface and then stops — that self-limiting step is what makes the thickness discrete and repeatable."],
    ["Outfeed and gauge","MEASURE","Thickness follows web speed: about 1 nm at 30 m/min, about 10 nm at 10 m/min. Slower means thicker, in whole atomic layers."]],
  params:["Coating thickness: 1 nm at 30 m/min, 10 nm at 10 m/min","Temperature: 100–250 °C","No vacuum required"],
  alts:["Vacuum and thin-film processes — PVD, CVD","Wet and dry coating"],
  chall:["Currently only for precursors with high vapour pressure","Complex surface structures"],
  qInf:["Web speed, which sets the number of cycles","Process temperature","Precursor vapour pressure"],
  qFeat:["Discrete adjustment of the layer thickness","Homogeneity and purity of the coating","Adhesion between coating and substrate"],
  sop:["Confirm the precursor has sufficient vapour pressure at the set temperature","Bring the chamber to 100–250 °C","Set web speed for the target film thickness","Purge between precursor zones and verify carry-over","Measure the film and confirm it is discrete, not graded","Release the coated layer to stacking"] },

{ id:"compacting", no:"12b", phase:"Cell assembly", title:"Isostatic compacting", machine:"compacting",
  routes:ALL, sub:"Cell assembly", trans:1, tpage:1,
  env:{iso:"Sealed press", dew:"dry", temp:"RT up to 2 000 °C"},
  cost:"—", takt:"holding time, seconds to hours",
  purpose:"Press the assembled layers together hard enough, and if necessary hot enough, that the porosity between them closes and the ions have a continuous path.",
  inp:"Loose layer stack", out:"Densified stack, layers in contact",
  parts:[
    ["Stack infeed","LOAD","The layers arrive loose. Until they are compacted, every interface between them is a resistance."],
    ["Isostatic press","COMPACT","Pressure from 5 to 600 MPa, temperature from room temperature up to 2 000 °C, held for anything from seconds to hours. Uniform heat penetration of the stack is the first named requirement — a cold core does not densify."],
    ["Densified stack","PRODUCT","Reduced porosity, higher ionic conductivity and adhesion between the cell layers. This is the step that turns a pile of layers into a cell."],
    ["Density gauge","MEASURE","Homogeneous compaction is the point. Compacting unevenly is worse than compacting lightly, because the thin spots become the short-circuit sites."]],
  params:["Uniform heat penetration of the stack","Pressure range: 5–600 MPa","Temperature range: RT–2 000 °C","Processing and holding time: seconds to hours"],
  alts:["The listed processes describe all practicable process alternatives."],
  chall:["Production speed","Prevention of short circuits, and damage-free compaction"],
  qInf:["Applied pressure","Temperature and how evenly it reaches the core","Holding time"],
  qFeat:["Reduced porosity","Increased ionic conductivity","Adhesion of the cell layers","Homogeneous compaction"],
  sop:["Confirm the stack is aligned before it is pressed","Set pressure, temperature and holding time for the electrolyte class","Bring the whole stack to temperature, not just its surface","Hold, then release under control","Measure relative density across the area, not at one point","Release only if compaction is even"] },

{ id:"slitting", no:"10", phase:"Electrode & electrolyte production", title:"Longitudinal slitting", machine:"slitting", routes:ALL,
  sub:"Cathode and electrolyte production", trans:4,
  env:{iso:"Dry / clean room", dew:"dry", temp:"ambient"},
  cost:"—", takt:"continuous",
  purpose:"Divide the wide electrode web into strips of the required width — the last step of electrode and electrolyte production.",
  inp:"Wide coated web", out:"Electrode strips",
  parts:[
    ["Web infeed","INFEED","The composite arrives from calendering or, on the oxide route, straight from deposition."],
    ["Laser head","CUT","Contactless. Separation without contact avoids the deflection, cracking and delamination that a knife can cause, and needs less maintenance."],
    ["Rolling knife","CUT","The mechanical alternative. Its forces can deflect the substrate and delaminate the coating — the reason laser is listed first here."],
    ["Guide rollers","SUPPORT","Hold the web through the cut so the edge geometry is repeatable."],
    ["Strips","PRODUCT","Clean cut edge, narrow evaporation notch and a low heat-affected zone are the three quality features."],
    ["Heat-affected zone","RISK","The laser's own risk: layer delamination, because the materials in the composite melt at different temperatures."]],
  params:["Cutting speed","Spot size","Pulse energy and duration","Pulse repetition rate","Laser power or line energy","Wavelength"],
  alts:["Punching"],
  qInf:["Fused-on parts, cracks and deflections","Decomposition products","Delamination of the coating"],
  qFeat:["Clean cut edge","Narrow evaporation notch","Low heat-affected zone"],
